<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meiji Restoration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Meiji Restoration was the political revolution of 1868 that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> and restored direct imperial rule under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-meiji">Emperor Meiji</a>. It launched a rapid programme of modernisation in government, industry and the military. The restoration marked the foundation of the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration.jpg" alt="Meiji Restoration" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Takahashi Yuichi (1828-1894) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Meiji_by_Takahashi_Yuichi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
